  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/... \nIssued at 1116 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nMonday through Wednesday, the surface high pressure will remain \nclose to the area, but far enough east to keep southerly winds \ngoing, but only at light levels. With highs in the 50s, clear skies \nor high / thin clouds, this will be a continuation of dry, \nseasonally pleasant weather into mid week.  Late week, a more \namplified upper pattern will bring stronger southerly flow to the \nMidwest.  With a deep trof potentially moving out of the Rockies \ntowards late week, this will offer some chance for rainfall in the \nregion.",
